  "planning_notes": [
    "Uno wiring preserved: PIR=D2 (digital input), DoorMagnet=D3 (digital input), LDR=A0 (analog input), Buzzer=D6 (tone output), Alarm LED=D13 (digital output), TM1637 CLK=D4/DIO=D5 (tm1637_number).",
    "Night auto-arming uses SysML logic based on LDR analog reading vs a model threshold (threshold/counters/timing handled in SysML, not in device requests).",
    "TM1637 displays event count during arming state when door opens and motion is detected; counting, wrap/reset, and invalid-command blanking handled in SysML.",
    "Serial uses baud 9600 and framing=implicit line_or_idle with idle_timeout_ms=20 as given; only command reception is requested here because no explicit STATUS report numeric/Boolean fields were provided.",
    "No PWM/audio/buzzer timing parameters are encoded in device requests; SysML uses elapsed_ms for real-time alarm/buzzer duration behavior."
